bugs:
- mobile browsers disagree on devicePixelRatio for the identical physical
  screen (measured on a Pixel 10: Chrome reports dpr=2.625 -> innerWidth 411,
  Firefox reports dpr=4 -> innerWidth 270 - both ~1080 physical px wide,
  since innerWidth*dpr is just the device's physical pixel width and is
  therefore consistent across browsers even when innerWidth alone isn't), so
  a viewport size derived from raw innerWidth/innerHeight alone shows
  meaningfully less content in Firefox than Chrome on the same device
  (clips anything sized to fit the Chrome-tuned viewport, e.g. a title
  headline). Fix: derive the viewport from physical pixels
  (innerWidth*devicePixelRatio, innerHeight*devicePixelRatio) instead of raw
  innerWidth/innerHeight, dividing by one project-chosen "physical px per
  world/CSS unit" density constant - this cancels the cross-browser dpr
  disagreement on any device, unlike unidrill's actual fix (game.js
  `resizeViewport()`/`MOBILE_REF_DPR`), which instead scales innerWidth by
  `devicePixelRatio / MOBILE_REF_DPR` with MOBILE_REF_DPR hardcoded to
  whatever Chrome happened to report on the one test phone - works for that
  device pairing but isn't the general form.

- inputs/pointer.js `isPointerUp()`: `pointerDownTime = 0 || true` parses as
  `pointerDownTime = (0 || true)` (`=` binds looser than `||`), so it assigns
  `true` instead of resetting to `0` - pointerDownTime never actually clears,
  so isPointerUp() (and isPointerDown()) keeps reading truthy on every frame
  after the first press/release. Harmless for a one-shot gate (bootGatePassed
  et al - the screen moves on before it's polled again), but re-triggers every
  frame on anything that stays on the same screen and reacts to a tap (e.g. a
  title-screen menu item toggled infinitely on a single click). Fix: add
  parens - `(pointerDownTime = 0) || true`.

credits:
